ft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   from the medial to the lateral end  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   B   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short double suture denoting the new margin  a short single suture the inferior and a long single suture the lateral  The new margin is marked with black ink  the opposing surface with blue ink  the medial aspect with green ink and the lateral aspect with yellow ink  On sectioning  no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   from the medial to the lateral aspect  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   C   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short double suture denoting the new margin  a short single suture the superior and a long single suture the lateral  The new margin is marked with blue ink  the opposing surface with black ink  the medial aspect with green ink and the lateral aspect with yellow ink  There is a previously opened  fragmented biopsy cavity on the opposing surface of the double short sutured margin  On sectioning  no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue and is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   from the superior to the inferior aspect  Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
