 by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 890 grams  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  and an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan unremarkable skin ellipse  Located medially on the superior aspect of the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a suture designating 12 o clock  The specimen is inked  anterior blue  posterior black   serially sectioned displaying a fairly well circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm mottled tan to tan pink to focally yellow  focally necrotic mass located in the lower outer quadrant  abutting the posterior inked margin  9 5cm from the superior  5 0cm from the inferior  13 5cm from the medial  7 5cm from the axillary tail  and 2 0cm from the anterior  The remaining cut surfaces focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty lobulated breast tissue  There are no other masses grossly identified or palpated  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections and the entire lymph nodes are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   A C  Mass to posterior black inked margin  D  Mass towards anterior margin  E  Representative sections of fibrous tissue lateral to the mass  F  Representative section of fibrous tissue medial to the mass  G J  Whole lymph nodes  K Q  One bisected lymph node each  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RADICAL MODIFIED MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 53 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  1   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN MANY AREAS  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  10    3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  The tumor is 1 2cm in diameter in histologic section  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The in situ component is present both within the infiltrating tumor and in sections separate from it  Immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  RIGHT  2   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   50   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  50    COMEDO TYPE  NOTE  The infiltrating tumor in this specimen is 0 8cm in diameter in histologic section  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one of the bulbous ends  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two yellow firm nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm in average size and focal gritty areas  one present around stitched tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Stitch area submitted in A and B  remainder submitted in C through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   2  is a 3 x 2 x 0 4cm mass of fibrofatty tissue  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue  fat  and a subtle faint nodularity  No frozen done  Specimen submitted entirely in K through N  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  WHITE 10 REPORTS TO  Bradley T Hyman  M D  Alik Farber  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 11 47 CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral breast mass with FNA suggestions of lymphoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  DIFFUSE LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SMALL FOCI  PROBABLY ARISING FROM A LOW GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  This case is unusual and is difficult to subclassify precisely  There is a dense nodular and diffuse lymphoid infiltrate  forming an ill defined mass and extensively involving the surrounding fat  The nodules vary in size and appear to have a lobular arrangement  consisting of peri acinar periductal proliferation of small lymphocytes admixed with many scattered transformed large lymphocytes  Some smaller nodules are vaguely defined and are composed of dense small to medium sized lymphocytes  some with descinable pale cytoplasm  Between nodules and in fat are large non cleaved lymphocytes in clusters or occasionally in sheets with admixed medium sized or small cells  Monotonous populations that are typical of centrocytes or marginal zone cells are not seen  Definitive follicular structures are not an obvious histologic feature  On morphologic grounds  the number of large atypical lymphocytes infiltrating the tissue is consistent  at least focally  with a diagnosis of large cell lymphoma  The lymphoid proliferation with singly distributed large cell component in many areas suggests that the large cell lymphoma may be associated with a low grade lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains on the paraffin section show that large cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     confirming the diagnosis of diffuse large B cell lymphoma  However  The B cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   arguing against the presence of a follicular or mantle cell lymphoma  see addendum   Although the extranodal location  the intimate association of lymphoid infiltrate with breast lobules and lack of large cell sheeting out tend to imply a lymphoma of mucosa associated lymphoid tissue  MALT  type  the histomorphology and immunophenotype are non specific and not sufficient to definitively subclassify the low grade component  Dr  Judith A  Ferry has reviewed the case the concurs with the diagnosis  Diagnosis by  HENRY DONG  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 07 58                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  FROZEN AND PARAFFIN SECTIONS  HP  REMOVED_CASE_ID    With antibodies to immunoglobulin there is a suggestion of monotypic  IgM Lambda  staining of many lymphoid cells in nodular and diffuse patterns  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most large cells and many small to medium sized cells  The B cells are negative for antibodies to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large cells are positive for Bcl 2  With antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of dendritic pattern within some small nodules  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of a B cell lymphoma and argue against mantle and follicular lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  HENRY DONG  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 23 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is unoriented fragment of yellow soft tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fatty tissue with a tan white nodular cut surface  A representative section is frozen as fx 1 and the frozen tissue is saved  Another section adjacent to frozen section  1 is fixed in B 5  and now submitted in cassette F  The remaining tissue is entirely submitted in cassette A E  Gross Description by  MANCONG ZHANG  MD Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LEFT  BREAST  HIGHLY ATYPICAL LYMPHOID INFILTRATE  CONSISTENT WITH MIXED SMALL CELL LARGE CELL MALIGNANT LYMPHOMA  O R  Resident  MANCONG ZHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISION , Unchecked.
