Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  MULTIFOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INVADING LYMPHATICS AND BLOOD VESSELS  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The largest tumor diameter is 3 7cm  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 28                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION OR BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   UNINTERPRETABLE SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    The assay was repeated 3 times  background was consistently high suggesting that there was a delay in tissue transport  that air drying occured  or that the tissue was not sent on wet ice  If S phase information is desired  flow cytometry should be attempted  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  10 MAY 93 at 11 09     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 46 fm mg cytosolic