Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 MAY 96 at 13 16 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  EXTENDING AWAY FROM MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 96 at 13 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy specimen and localizing wire  The specimen has been inked and sectioned to reveal a firm grey white 0 9cm area  Frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted in total in cassette A through G with suspicious area in cassettes A through C  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  FIRM AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Masha Jannine Etkin  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
