Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 37 CLINICAL DATA  57 year old white female with a large  8 0cm   tumor of the left breast  status post chemotherapy preoperatively                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  Note  The margins of resection appear free of carcinoma  The invasive carcinoma is at least 12 0cm and is present in all 13 slides  Blood vascular invasion is not seen  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 4 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTRANODAL SOFT TISSUE EXTENSION PRESENT IN ALL 4 POSITIVE NODES  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU 4  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS 5  FIBROADENOMA  MICROSCOPIC 6  HEALING BIOSPY SITE Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen which includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm attached axillary tail  A REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse overlies the specimen  and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple alveolar complex  located 4 5cm from the inferior superior margin  A 2 5cm  well healed scar is present superior to the nipple  located 6 5cm from the medial and superior skin margins  The deep surface is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm ill defined  tan yellow  mass located in the upper inner quadrant  extending to within 0 4cm of the closest deep soft tissue margin and 1 5cm from the superomedial soft tissue margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains several ill defined fibrotic areas  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  located in the lower inner quadrant  extending to within 1 5cm of the closest deep margin and 2 0cm of the closest inferomedial soft tissue margin  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrotic biopsy cavity surrounded by bright yellow breast parenchyma is identified subjacent to the skin scar  located 3cm from the deep margin and 8cm from the superior margin  The attached axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple  tan  ovoid  soft lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  Section code  A  nipple B  skin with scar and underlying biopsy cavity C D firm area with closest deep resection margin E J firm area  representative sections K M fibrotic area  representative sections N R lymph nodes Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Vikram S Kashyap  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    AXILLA  LEFT  , Unchecked.
