Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11 14 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer invasive lobular carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  LYMPH NODES   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 20 45                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision left breast cancer  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm irregular tan yellow to pink portion of fibrofatty tissue with a single suture designating the superior aspect and a double suture designating the lateral aspect  The superior aspect is inked green  inferior yellow  anterior blue and posterior black  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm irregular tan white skin ellipse along the anterior aspect with a 3 0cm linear well healed scar  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm biopsy cavity with firm  focally hemorrhagic cavity wall  The cavity comes to 0 5cm from the inferior aspect  1 0cm from the posterior  0 6cm from the superior  3 0cm from skin surface  2 2cm from the medial and 3 6cm from the lateral aspect  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm well delineated tan pink rubbery area located along the postero inferior aspect of the cavity wall  coming to 0 3cm of the inferior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm ill defined  fibrous  irregular tan white area located along the anterior aspect of the cavity wall  coming to 0 9cm from the skin surface  1 1cm and 1 2cm from the inferior and superior margins respectively  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A H as follows  A  Well delineated area along postero inferior cavity wall  B E  Representative sections of cavity wall  F  Uninvolved parenchyma  G H  Ill defined fibrous area along anterior aspect of wall  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  are two irregular tan pink lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The lymph nodes are bisected to reveal a smooth homogenous tan pink cut surface  The larger node is entirely submitted in cassette J and the smaller in cassette I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm of irregular tan pink to yellow portion of fibrofatty tissue  No lymph nodes are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette K  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  NICOLE ANN BELSLEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 AUG 94 at 13 22 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal calcifications on mammogram with a prior lobular carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  A SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  SLIDE C  WHICH IS REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIMENSION AND EXTENDS TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and vascular invasion is not identified  2 LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL FOCI  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM INKED SURFACES  3 RADIAL SCAR  MICROSCOPIC  4 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  INTRALOBULAR FIBROSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 19 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 19     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm red and yellow soft mass with axial needle and focal firmness  It is inked and sectioned to reveal an extensive white area with punctate hemorrhage against a yellow background  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F    A  represents the nearest needle base   F  represents the nearest needle point  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   NO OBVIOUS INVASIVE CARCINOMA GROSSLY  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Unchecked.
