Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 22 CLINICAL DATA  Status post breast cancer  right  in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW NUCLEAR GRADE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  SIMPLE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND MICROCYSTS HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone r