_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy with a short stitch superior and long stitch lateral  The anterior is inked blue  and the posterior is inked black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm tan skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple areolar complex  which is grossly unremarkable  Sectioning reveals that in the lateral breast there are multiple areas of firm  ill defined pink tissue  approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm located 0 5cm from the anterior margin and 3 0cm from the posterior margin  More medial in the breast there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm poorly circumscribed  white tan fibrous to hemorrhagic area located 3 5cm from the anterior margin and 5 5cm from the posterior margin  there is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm rubbery to firm  pink tan  well circumscribed area located 2 5cm from the anterior margin and 3 0cm from the posterior margin  possibly representing a previous biopsy site  The remaining parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm areas of the lateral breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  includes anterior margin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  include posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region of possible previous biopsy site  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy flap  are four sections of skin and underlying subcutaneous tissue  The first is triangular and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  the second measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  the third measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and the fourth measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The skin surface is tan without lesions or masses  Representative sections from each piece are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_P