  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Seven specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm incision of breast biopsy with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Inferior is yellow  superior is red  lateral is blue  medial is green  anterior and posterior are black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate gritty mass present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  Mass is submitted in cassettes A through C with anterior  black   lateral  blue   and posterior  black overinked in yellow   Needle localization site  slightly firm no gross tumor  and anterior margin are submitted in D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are the 6 remaining specimens  Labeled as  left breast  additional anterior 