ith a suture at the possible axillary tail aspect  On the anterior aspect  is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm oval tan white unremarkable portion of skin with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable nipple  No scar is grossly appreciated  The anterior aspect is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an indurated  ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mass which is located centrally between the upper outer and upper inner quadrants  coming to 2 5cm from the posterior  and 1 3cm from the anterior soft tissue margin  Abutting the mass  anteriorly  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm cavity filled with hemorrhagic dark red clotted blood  possible previous core biopsy site that extends to 1 2cm from the anterior soft tissue margin and 3 7cm from the posterior margin  Located 3 2cm inferiorly is an additional hemorrhagic cystic mass which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and is filled with dark red clotted blood  this mass extends to less than 0 2cm from the anterior margin  The intervening parenchyma between the aforementioned large mass and the cyst cavity is tan yellow  lobulated with no mass identified  The overall measurement of the aforementioned mass and the cyst cavity with indurated borders measures 7 0cm superior to inferior  2 5cm from anterior to posterior  and 2 0cm from medial to lateral  The remaining parenchyma predominantly consists of nodular gray dense fibrous tissue containing multiple cystic structures filled with cloudy tan fluid averaging 0 2cm in diameter  No additional masses or lesions are identified  Within the possible area sutured located within the axillary tail region  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Also received detached from the specimen  and in the same container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of tan white unremarkable skin with up to 1 0cm of attached tan yellow lobulated unremarkable subcutaneous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin taken en face to largest primary nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Primary mass to include abutting anterior possible core biopsy cavity and anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of primary mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening parenchyma between primary mass and additional more inferior cyst cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire more inferior cyst cavity to anterior aspect with surrounding indurated borders   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma taken lateral to aforementioned areas within dense cystic fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of detached skin and subcutaneous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of firm tissue adjacent to inferior cavity  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY   report_end  , Unchecked.
