 margin  3 5cm from the medial margin and 0 3cm subadjacent to the anterior overlying skin ellipse  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of white  smooth  rubbery breast tissue with a few areas of yellow  soft  lobulated fat  SECTION CODE  A  inferior margin  radial section B  deep margin with cavity  radial section C  superior margin  radial section D  lateral margin  en face E  medial margin  en face F  anterior margin  skin with cavity G K  biopsy cavity  representative sections L N  breast parenchyma  representative sections Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two separate parts  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of yellow red  fibrofatty breast tissue with multiple  firm  palpable lymph nodes  The specimen is dissected to reveal twenty lymph nodes which range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 4cm in greatest dimension and have cut surfaces that range from fleshy tan to soft yellow to speckled yellow  The smaller nodes are submitted entirely  while one representative section of the larger nodes is submitted  O V  lymph nodes  left axilla  Labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is bisected to reveal THREE lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm in greatest dimension  having a fleshy tan to homogeneously white and firm cut surface  One half of the entire sample is submitted in W  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  COMPLETELY EXCISED BIOPSY CAVITY COMING WITHIN 0 2CM OF DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
