ase and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast excision specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect  a long suture designating the lateral aspect  and two localization wires  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal two stellate tan white scars  The first lies 2 0cm from the medial margin  1 2cm from superior margin  3 0cm from the anterior margin  2 0cm from the inferior margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and 5 0cm from lateral margin  The second scar lies 6 5cm lateral to the first biopsy site  7 0cm from the medial margin  0 6cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  2 0cm from the posterior margin  1 8cm from the inferior margin  and 0 7cm from the lateral margin  Approximately 1 4cm lateral to the first biopsy site is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fairly well demarcated  tan white  rubbery nodule  The breast parenchyma between the two scars is tan white  rubbery  and firm  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first biopsy site with closest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second biopsy site with closest site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  tan white  rubbery nodule with closest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening breast parenchyma between the scars   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  medial margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section  lateral margin Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  FSM left breast inferior  are multiple pieces of unoriented tan yellow  lobulated adipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  which are sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOV