st to the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm   tan white  firm  stellate lesion with a central REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  cystic and hemorrhagic cavity  extends to the skin surface  anterior margin  and focally to the superior and inferior margins  and is located 1 5cm  from the medial margin  2 5cm  from the lateral margin  and 0 5cm  from the deep margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm   white  round  ovoid  rubbery  firm area separate from the main mass  located 0 2cm  from the deep margin  0 2cm  from the superior margin  1 8cm  from the inferior margin  1 2cm  from the anterior margin  2cm  from the medial margin  and 3 5cm  from the lateral margin  There is a third lesion  that is round  white  and papillary  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   and located subadjacent to the superior resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  soft  lobulated  and interspersed with thin  white  rubbery  shiny fibrous bands  Labeled  B  axilla  is a 8 x 6 x 1 5cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from less than 0 1cm  to 0 3cm  greatest dimension  Each lymph node is submitted entirely  The remaining fibroadipose tissue is also entirely submitted  Section code  A Medial margin  en face  B Lateral margin  en face  C Inferior margin  radial section  D Superior margin  radial section  E Deep margin  radial section  F Anterior margin  skin with tumor  radial section  G H Rubbery nodule  I Papillary nodule  J L Biopsy cavity  entirely  N Q Breast parenchyma surrounding biopsy cavity  representative sections  R S Breast parenchyma  representative sections  T Y Axillary lymph nodes  Z AN Axillary fibroadipose tissue  entirely  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART